Description
-----------
This module introduces the Python List data structure.

A list is an ordered, mutable collection that can store
multiple values in a single variable. A list can contain
different data types, including integers, strings,
floating-point numbers, Boolean values, and even other
lists.

Lists are one of the most frequently used data structures
in Python because they are flexible, easy to use, and
well suited for storing collections of related data.

Learning Objectives
-------------------
1. Understand what a list is.
2. Learn how to create a list.
3. Access list elements using indexes.
4. Add new elements to a list.
5. Modify existing elements.
6. Remove elements from a list.
7. Iterate through a list using a for loop.
8. Display list information clearly.

Functions Used
--------------
print()     Display information.
len()       Return the number of items.
append()    Add an item to the end of a list.
remove()    Remove an item by value.

Expected Output
---------------
The program demonstrates how to create, access, update,
add, remove, and display list elements.

Coding Style
------------
This module follows clean code principles and PEP 8
recommendations for readability, maintainability,
and professional software development.
=========================================================
"""


def display_header():
    """Display the program title."""

    print("=" * 70)
    print("Python Lists")
    print("=" * 70)


def display_list(title, items):
    """Display all elements in a list."""

    print()
    print(title)
    print("-" * 70)

    for index, item in enumerate(items, start=1):
        print(f"{index}. {item}")


def main():
    """Main entry point of the program."""

    display_header()

    # =====================================================
    # Create List
    # =====================================================

    programming_languages = [
        "Python",
        "Java",
        "C++",
        "JavaScript"
    ]

    # =====================================================
    # Access List Element
    # =====================================================

    first_language = programming_languages[0]

    # =====================================================
    # Add New Element
    # =====================================================

    programming_languages.append("Go")

    # =====================================================
    # Modify Element
    # =====================================================

    programming_languages[2] = "C#"

    # =====================================================
    # Remove Element
    # =====================================================

    programming_languages.remove("Java")

    # =====================================================
    # Display Results
    # =====================================================

    print(f"First Language : {first_language}")
    print(f"Total Items    : {len(programming_languages)}")

    display_list(
        "Programming Languages",
        programming_languages
    )

    print()
    print("=" * 70)
    print("Program Completed Successfully")
    print("=" * 70)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
